        'Late 20th century: Often compared with FreeCell in solitaire literature, though it remains stricter and less forgiving.',
      ],
      evolution: "The game's harsh 'no empty cell' rule led to variants like 'Streets and Alleys' (Citadel) which place the Aces in the tableau to ease the opening.",
