          deckDescription: 'One standard 52-card deck consisting of four suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs), each with thirteen ranks from ace down to two. No jokers; used for Beleaguered Castle solitaire where the four aces start in the center and building is by suit in descending order.',
          suitDescription: 'Four French suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs). The four aces form the foundations and build up in suit (ace to king). Tableau piles build down in suit (e.g. seven on eight). All four suits are used.',
          rankDescription: 'Thirteen ranks per suit. On foundations, building is ace (low) to king (high) in the same suit. In the tableau, building is descending by suit (king down to two). Standard solitaire ranking for Beleaguered Castle.',
          dealPattern: 'Aces removed first, then 48 cards dealt into eight piles of six.',
          bettingLimits: 'None',
          actions: {},
          handRankingSystem: 'None; rank is used for sequence building rather than comparative strength.',
          rankingSystem: 'Foundation Build',
